# {{task_name}} Research Architecture

Generated by {{skill_name}} v{{skill_version}}.

## Purpose

Separate maintained research code, data contracts, configurations, environments, execution surfaces, generated artifacts, and evidence so the task can be reproduced and reviewed.

## Responsibility Map

| Area | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `src/{{package_name}}/` | Maintained task-specific research code |
| `data_contracts/` | Input identity, schema, split, availability, and permitted-use contracts; no datasets by default |
| `configs/` | Reviewable experiment and method configurations |
| `environment/` | Reproducible local or remote environment specifications |
| `scripts/` | Repeatable task entrypoints and bounded utilities |
| `notebooks/` | Exploration with explicit inputs, outputs, and promotion rules |
| `tests/` | Contract, unit, leakage, integration, and smoke checks as applicable |
| `research_artifacts/` | Generated outputs or references to approved external storage |
| `running_logs/` | Generated runtime logs, normally untracked |
| `evidence/` | Compact evidence and receipts supporting research claims |
| `reports/` | Reviewed synthesis and evaluation claims |

## Intended Flow

```text
sources and data identity
          |
          v
protocol and contracts -> maintained code + configuration + environment
          |                                  |
          +----------------+-----------------+
                           v
                    bounded execution
                           |
                           v
                 artifacts + evidence -> reports
```

## Evidence Boundary

An import, unit test, or smoke run is engineering evidence. Comparative or research-quality claims require the accepted protocol, eligible runs, metrics, and limitations.

